                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\pi}^{(i)}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            functor in the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^{th}
            direction. Using this expression of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi n
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_n X
            one can check that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
